  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe utilizes 3 medium food storage containers.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a large pot over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the pot heats up, peel, halve, and small dice onion. Peel and mince garlic.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ medium yellow onion\n2 clove garlic"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the pot is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add onion, garlic, pork sausage, and spices; cook, breaking the meat apart with a spoon, until pork is cooked through and onion is tender, 5-6 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 tsp extra virgin olive oil\n340 g ground pork sausage\n¾ tsp paprika\n¾ tsp Italian seasoning\n½ tsp salt"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash, dry, and large dice potatoes. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Drain and rinse beans.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (442 g) can cannellini (white kidney) beans"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the pork and onions are done, add potatoes, beans, broth, and water to the pot. Stir to combine the soup and bring to a simmer over medium-high heat. Once simmering, reduce heat to medium and cook, stirring occasionally, until potatoes are tender, 10-12 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "4 cups chicken or vegetable broth"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the soup is cooking, wash and dry kale. Fold leaves in half lengthwise and slice off the stems; chop or tear leaves into bite-sized pieces.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 bunch kale"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the potatoes are tender, add kale to the pot in handfuls, waiting for it to wilt slightly before adding the next handful. Add cream, stir to combine, and continue to cook until kale is tender, 2-3 minutes more. Remove from heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ cup heavy whipping cream"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Divide soup between the storage containers, then set aside to cool completely, about 1 hour. Once cool, cover containers and refrigerate. When ready to eat, heat soup in a saucepan or microwave and enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
